1
00:00:00,298 --> 00:00:02,388
(Penny:)No. Yeah, I remember specifically.

2
00:00:02,551 --> 00:00:07,351
(Penny:)You started by asking if I was from Mars
because my ass was out of this world.

3
00:00:09,975 --> 00:00:12,355
(Howard:)Well, that does sound like me, but no.

4
00:00:13,603 --> 00:00:14,813
SHELDON:
Is there some problem?

5
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:18,980
Yeah, um, listen,
I have to kind of sneak out for a while.

6
00:00:19,442 --> 00:00:22,442
- All right. Goodbye.
- No, wait.

7
00:00:22,612 --> 00:00:25,202
(Leonard:)If anyone asks you where I went,
you don't know.

8
00:00:25,365 --> 00:00:28,285
- Where are you going?
- I can't tell you that.

9
00:00:29,035 --> 00:00:30,745
Well, who would ask me?

10
00:00:31,830 --> 00:00:34,000
(Leonard:)I can't tell you that either.

11
00:00:34,666 --> 00:00:37,876
You brought me here to inform me
you can't tell me where you're going.

12
00:00:38,044 --> 00:00:40,754
(Sheldon:)And you can't tell me who might ask?

13
00:00:42,173 --> 00:00:45,013
(Leonard:)Yeah, I really didn't think this through.

14
00:00:46,928 --> 00:00:48,968
- Leonard, a moment.
- What?

15
00:00:49,139 --> 00:00:51,469
(Sheldon:)If someone...
And we don't know who this would be.

16
00:00:51,641 --> 00:00:54,061
(Sheldon:)...does ask where you've gone,
what should I say?

17
00:00:54,227 --> 00:00:56,477
(Howard:)I don't know.
Tell them I went to the office.

18
00:00:56,646 --> 00:00:58,396
- Are you going to the office?
- No.

19
00:00:58,565 --> 00:01:02,775
- Well, then how can I say it convincingly?
- Just say, "Leonard went to the office."

